---
/** How to read the labels, and where the assessment content comes from. */
import GuideLabel from './GuideLabel.astro';
---

<aside class="lk" aria-labelledby="lk-h">
  <h2 id="lk-h" class="lk__h">How to read the labels</h2>
  <dl class="lk__list">
    <div><dt><GuideLabel kind="ib" /></dt><dd>From the IB Business management guide or the IB's examiner instructions.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><GuideLabel kind="examiner" /></dt><dd>What IB subject reports (May 2024 to May 2026) say examiners reward or penalize, as cited in the assessment guides.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><GuideLabel kind="strategy" /></dt><dd>A technique the platform recommends. It is not an IB rule.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><GuideLabel kind="example" /></dt><dd>Invented for teaching: the businesses, figures and answers are fictional.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="lk__src">
    Built from the Arjun Agrawal Knowledge Series assessment guides (IA, Paper 1, Paper 2, Paper 3), which cite the IB guide (first assessment 2024),
    the IB teacher support material and IB subject reports. Facts about the IB course were checked against the guide itself, with its pages; the subject
    reports were not supplied to this platform, so examiner emphasis is given as the guides state it. Nothing here predicts a grade or approves a piece of
    work.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .lk {
    padding: var(--sp-5);
    background: var(--surface-sheet);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--navy-900);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sheet);
  }

  .lk__h {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .lk__list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-5);
    margin: var(--sp-4) 0 0;
  }

  .lk__list dd {
    margin: var(--sp-2) 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .lk__src {
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
    padding-top: var(--sp-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-hair);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
